## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design a practical streaming PCA workflow suitable for beginners, focusing on:
- Online dimensionality reduction techniques
- Missing data handling in streaming contexts
- Component selection strategies
- Translating statistical outputs into actionable alerts
- Meeting strict latency requirements

## Key Concepts

- **IncrementalPCA**: Ideal for streaming data with mini-batch updates, allowing real-time adaptation
- **Missing Data Imputation**: Simple mean imputation maintains speed while handling occasional gaps
- **Component Selection**: Explained variance threshold (>90%) provides automated dimensionality decision
- **Loadings Interpretation**: High-loading features drive deterministic alert generation
- **Latency Optimization**: Efficient batch processing ensures sub-5ms transaction processing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simplified online PCA implementation
// Initialize IncrementalPCA with 6 components
const pca = new IncrementalPCA(n_components: 6, batch_size: 1000);

// Process streaming transactions
function processTransaction(transaction) {
  // Impute missing values with feature means
  const cleanData = imputeMissing(transaction, featureMeans);

  // Project to lower dimension
  const components = pca.partial_fit(cleanData);

  // Generate alerts from top loadings
  return generateAlerts(components, loadings);
}
```

